('lewis-emperor','Lewis the Emperor','A Frankish emperor in Canterbury’s pedigree, son of Charlemagne.','Lewis the Emperor','person'),
('lewis-tenth','King Lewis the Tenth','The French king who wore the crown uneasily until his descent through the female line satisfied him.','King Lewis the Tenth|Lewis the Tenth','person'),
('isabel-grandmother','Queen Isabel','King Lewis the Tenth’s grandmother in Canterbury’s pedigree; a different Queen Isabel from the French queen in the play.','','person'),
('alexander-the-great','Alexander the Great','The Macedonian king, whom Fluellen compares to King Henry.','Alexander the Great|Alexander the Pig|Alexander','person'),
('philip-of-macedon','Philip of Macedon','Alexander the Great’s father.','Philip of Macedon','person'),
('cleitus','Cleitus','The friend Alexander killed in drink.','Cleitus','person'),
('pompey-the-great','Pompey the Great','The Roman general whose camp Fluellen holds up as a model of discipline.','Pompey the Great|Pompey','person'),
('mark-antony','Mark Antony','The Roman commander Fluellen names as a byword for valour.','Mark Antony','person'),
('agamemnon','Agamemnon','The Greek commander at Troy, Fluellen’s measure of greatness of soul.','Agamemnon','person'),
