('brutus','Brutus','The Roman who hid his purpose under an appearance of folly.','Brutus','person'),
('herod','Herod','The king of Judea whose soldiers killed the children, in King Henry’s threat to Harfleur.','Herod','person'),
('adam','Adam','The first man, whose offending nature the Archbishop says was whipped out of the King.','Adam','religious-figure'),
('arthur','Arthur','King Arthur; the Hostess puts Falstaff in “Arthur’s bosom”, meaning Abraham’s.','Arthur','literary-figure'),
